---
date added: 2026-11-08
title: Basic Baked Potatoes
author: Florence Fabricant
source: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/8266-basic-baked-potatoes
tags: potato, side dish, butter, five ingredient, for one
servings: 1
time required: 1 hour
cook time: 1 hour
---

Preheat oven to 450 degrees.

Scrub the @oval baking potatoes{1}(or more), dry them and, if desired, rub the skin of each with a teaspoon of @butter or vegetable oil{1%teaspoon}(or more). Prick the skin of each potato in one or two places with a fork or with the point of a knife.

Place the potatoes in the oven and bake ~{45-60%minutes}, until the potato offers no resistance when a knife is inserted in the center.

Remove the potatoes from the oven and serve at once, whole, or score the potato or potatoes with an X, squeeze the sides of the potato to force the X open and serve.
